    {
      "title": "In the Tunnel",
      "desc": "The proxy copies, unread",
      "detail": "From now on the proxy copies bytes both ways without reading them. The browser’s TLS Client Hello goes in on the laptop’s connection and comes out, byte for byte the same, on the proxy’s connection to the server. TLS runs from end to end, so the proxy learns the site’s name and the sizes, never the pages. (Some company proxies do open HTTPS, using a certificate authority installed on every company laptop; then they see everything.)",
      "facts": [
        [
          "Proxy sees",
          "Site name, sizes, timing"
        ],
        [
          "Hidden from it",
          "Pages, passwords, cookies"
        ],
        [
          "Encryption",
          "TLS, laptop to server"
        ]
      ],
